This is a ROM framework integration, not the HMA-OSS Zygisk module.
It does not require Zygisk or LSPosed. Configuration is stored per Android
user in Settings.Secure/unica_hma_policy and applies only to selected callers.
Logging is off by default; the viewer filters this user's recent UnicaHMA
logcat events. Installer spoofing is not part of this implementation.

Java sources are retained under src/. Generated smali is distributed as patches
under this mod and the Settings mod. Compile with Java 8 bytecode, D8 min API 26,
then disassemble with the project's baksmali. Do not package compile-only stubs.
tools/rebuild.sh reproduces the three generated patches in a new /tmp directory
and backs up existing patches before replacement. It requires local android.jar,
json.jar and r8.jar inputs (validated with Android 4.1.1.4 compile stubs,
org.json 20240303 and R8/D8 8.3.37). Dependencies are not included in the ROM.
tests/run.sh runs host preset and settings replacement tests with local inputs.
Host tests and DEX assembly do not establish on-device behavior.
The Settings fragment retains its previous registered class name for gateway
compatibility. The old Global settings getter hook is retired to prevent it
from overriding the new per-caller settings policy.
